# gradlew is a POSIX shell script executed directly (./gradlew, and the
# Dockerfile's `RUN ./gradlew`). A CRLF checkout breaks its shebang under any
# strict /bin/sh - Alpine's BusyBox ash included - with "gradlew: not found",
# because the interpreter path becomes "/bin/sh\r". The committed blob is LF;
# this file is what keeps every checkout that way, including a Windows one
# with core.autocrlf=true.
#
# Scoped to the wrapper only, deliberately: a blanket `* text=auto eol=lf`
# would renormalize every other tracked file's line endings too, which is
# unrelated to this fix and would show up as unrelated churn.
gradlew text eol=lf
gradlew.bat text eol=crlf
gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar binary
